      "side": 1,
      "message": "The primary intent is to establish a direct D-Bus association between a software updater object and its corresponding sensor configuration.\n\nTo achieve this while adhering to the Entity-Manager device modeling architecture advised in dbus-sensors/+/83968, devices like I2C VRs are modeled as a single top-level hardware type (e.g., `Type: MP29612`) rather than splitting them into separate sensor and firmware configs.\n\nBecause they are consolidated into a single configuration, the resulting D-Bus interface is specific to the sensor\u0027s hardware model (e.g., `xyz.openbmc_project.Configuration.MP29612`). Consequently, the Software Manager dynamically discovers these hardware-specific interfaces rather than relying on hardcoded lists.\n\nOnce discovered, the Software Manager attaches a `configures` association directly to the shared EM configuration object. This provides the critical link that allows psusensor to map sensors to its firmware updater.",
